---
const repo = "https://github.com/sachncs/methodos";
const items = [["01", "Locate", "Match the last action to the part of the graph that matters now."], ["02", "Guide", "Turn the local neighbourhood into concise, cached guidance."], ["03", "Refine", "Score runs, propose edits, and keep only validated improvements."]];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" /><meta name="theme-color" content="#f5f4ef" /><meta name="description" content="A typed procedural memory for LLM agents." /><meta property="og:title" content="methodos — procedural memory for agents" /><meta property="og:description" content="Inspectable, local procedural memory for agents that need to get better." /><meta property="og:type" content="website" /><meta property="og:url" content="https://sachncs.github.io/methodos/" /><link rel="canonical" href="https://sachncs.github.io/methodos/" /><title>methodos — procedural memory for agents</title><link rel="icon" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}favicon.svg`} /></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="#top"><span class="mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>methodos</a><nav><a href="#loop">The loop</a><a href="#architecture">Architecture</a><a href="#start">Start here</a></nav><a href={repo}>View source ↗</a></header>
<main id="top"><section class="hero wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">● Open source · Python · Apache-2.0</p><h1>Give your agent<br /><em>a way forward.</em></h1><p class="lede">Methodos is a typed procedural memory for LLM agents. It turns execution feedback into a graph of better next steps — inspectable, local, and built to stay out of your way.</p><a class="button" href={`${repo}#readme`}>Read the docs ↗</a><a class="link" href="#loop">See how it works ↓</a></div><div class="visual"><small>procedural memory</small><svg viewBox="0 0 560 500" aria-label="Procedural graph"><circle cx="280" cy="250" r="120" fill="#f5f4ef" stroke="#d9d8d0"/><circle cx="280" cy="250" r="58" fill="#131414"/><circle cx="280" cy="250" r="16" fill="#c9f25f"/><g fill="none" stroke="#77786f" stroke-width="2"><path d="M100 110C180 110 200 190 238 216M460 110C380 110 360 190 322 216M100 390C180 390 200 310 238 284M460 390C380 390 360 310 322 284"/></g><g fill="#f5f4ef" stroke="#131414" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="90" cy="100" r="11"/><circle cx="470" cy="100" r="11"/><circle cx="90" cy="400" r="11"/><circle cx="470" cy="400" r="11"/></g><g font-family="monospace" font-size="12" fill="#66675f"><text x="60" y="75">context</text><text x="438" y="75">action</text><text x="50" y="435">observe</text><text x="420" y="435">refine</text></g></svg><small>what to do next</small></div></section>
<section class="signals"><div class="wrap"><span>QUERYABLE</span><span>LOCALIZED</span><span>VALIDATED</span><span>EVOLVING</span></div></section>
<section id="loop" class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">The loop</p><h2>Useful in the hot path.<br /><span>Improving off the hot path.</span></h2><p class="lede">Runtime guidance stays separate from offline evolution, so experimentation never touches the live graph.</p><div class="cards">{items.map(([n, title, text]) => <article><b>{n}</b><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p><code>{title.toLowerCase()}(graph)</code></article>)}</div></section>
<section id="architecture" class="dark"><div class="wrap two"><div><p class="eyebrow">A small core</p><h2>One primitive.<br /><span>Clear boundaries.</span></h2><p class="lede">Data contracts, pure graph operations, replaceable protocols, and explicit persistence. Read the whole thing. Change the part you need.</p></div><div class="modules">{["schema.py", "graph.py", "adapter.py", "evolution.py", "repo.py", "service.py"].map((name, i) => <a href={`${repo}/blob/master/methodos/${name}`}>0{i + 1}　{name} <small>↗</small></a>)}</div></div></section>
<section id="start" class="section wrap two"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start here</p><h2>Keep the agent.<br /><span>Add the method.</span></h2><p class="lede">Bring your own solver. Methodos speaks through a small async protocol, so the graph can sit beside the agent you already have.</p><a class="button" href={repo}>Explore the repository ↗</a></div><pre><code>$ pip install methodos<br /><br /><span>from</span> methodos <span>import</span> PGAdapter<br /><br />adapter = PGAdapter(...)</code></pre></section></main>
<footer class="wrap"><a class="brand" href="#top"><span class="mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>methodos</a><span>Procedural memory for agents that need to get better.</span><span><a href={repo}>GitHub ↗</a>　<a href={`${repo}/blob/master/LICENSE`}>Apache-2.0 ↗</a></span></footer></body></html>
<style>
